X-ray images of COVID-19 patients contain valuable information about disease severity, which can influence ICU admission decisions. This study proposes a new concept - spitziness, measured by the Multi-Dimensional Scale method, to evaluate lung condition in X-ray images. Three methods for automatically calculating spitziness have been developed and tested against expert ratings from two separate datasets. Our experiments indicate that spitziness correlates strongly with disease severity, making it a valuable criterion for deciding ICU admission. Furthermore, we investigated the impact of spitziness on ICU admission decisions using machine learning algorithms, incorporating clinical data and spitziness ratings. Our analysis suggests that ICU admission decisions are influenced not only by clinical data but also by spitziness ratings. To verify these findings, we conducted expert consultations, revealing that spitziness ratings align with experts' decisions. Ultimately, we demonstrated that automatic spitziness calculation and ICU admission decision-making are feasible with limited supervision. Our approach contributes to developing more accurate automated systems for decision-making in COVID-19 care. The code for this research is available on GitHub at https://github.com/uchicago-covid19/Spitziness. The generated data can be accessed on Mimir at https://mimir.uchicago.edu/. The X-ray image data used in this study can be found on Chest X-Ray COVID-19 at https://github.com/thisayc/covid-19. Expert ratings and corresponding clinical data are available on Mimir at https://mimir.uchicago.edu/. 

\textit{Note: This research was conducted in Spring 2021 in Dr. Yashar M. Golan's course at the University of Chicago under the supervision of Dr. Golan.} 

\textit{Confidence level: 0.9} 

\textit{Limitation: This research is constrained by the limited scope of a semester-long course and lacks extensive expert consultations to further validate spitziness as a critical criterion for ICU admission decisions. Additional data and expert input would be necessary to further establish spitziness as a decisive factor in ICU admission decisions.} 

